6558\" line doesn't start with whitespace? It starts with \"SubTotal:\". The next line \"Total: $6558\" starts with \"Total:\". So use multiline `(?m)^Total:`.\n- amount_due = regex `Amount due:\\s*\\$?\\s*([\\d,]+)`.\n- Since they differ (6558 vs 4382), use Total.\n\nPDF-style:\n- `(?m)^\\s*TotalPrice\\s+([\\d.]+)` — note OCR text \"TotalPrice   896.0\". Good. Also \"Total Price:\\s*440.0\" (Ld, not invoice).\n\nVAT-style:\n- The \"Gross worth\" line. In OCR:\n  - 6fAoBvWIKKol: \"...Gross worth\\n\\n819,06\\n\\n$ 819,06\"\n  - UhfjWeF1yWim: \"...Gross worth\\n\\n797,91\\n\\n$ 797,91\"\n  - aWSjlbEKQFUY: \"...Gross worth\\n44 745,59\\n\\n$ 44 745,59\"\n  - omNO9OZCH_Uz: \"...Gross worth\\n10% 5 640,17 564,02 6 204,19\\n\\nTotal $5 640,17 $ 564,02 $ 6 204,19\"\n  - ovgnAeHA4rlK: \"...Gross worth\\n\\n6 860,45\\n\\n$ 6 860,45\"\n\nSo the occurrence of \"Gross worth\" is followed by a line with the numbers. In omNO9OZCH, \"Gross worth\" header is followed by \"10% 5 640,17 564,02 6 204,19\". Hmm. Maybe better to extract all \"$\" amount lines and take the last \"$ ...\" amount as gross-worth total. Let's examine the \"$\" lines:\n\n6fAoBvWIKKol:\n```\n$ 744,60\n$ 819,06  <- wait where does this appear? OCR:\n\"Net worth\n744,60\n\n$ 744,60\n\nNet worth VAT [%] ... VAT\n74,46\n\n$ 74,46\n\nGross ...\n819,06\n\n$ 819,06\"\n```\nActually the OCR line at \"SUMMARY\" section: \n```\nSUMMARY\n\nVAT [%]\n10%\n\nTotal\n\n...\nNet worth\n744,60\n\n$ 744,60\n\nNet worth VAT [%]\n179,96 10%\n...\nVAT\n74,46\n\n$ 74,46\n\nGross\nworth\n\n819,06\n\n$ 819,06\n```\n\nSo \"$ 819,06\" is the last \"$\" amount. The last dollar amount in the document = gross total. Similarly:\n- UhfjWeF1yWim: last \"$ 797,91\"\n- aWSjlbEKQFUY: last \"$ 44 745,59\"\n- omNO9OZCH_Uz: last amounts: \"Total $5 640,17 $ 564,02 $ 6 204,19\" → last \"$ 6 204,19\"\n- ovgnAeHA4rlK: last \"$ 6 860,45\"\n\nSo for VAT-style invoices, total = last \"$\" amount. But that also works for Stripe-style ones: last \"$\" amo